      "text": [
        ": «إِنَّ اَللَّهَ تَبَارَكَ وَ تَعَالَى قَرَنَ اَلزَّكَاةَ بِالصَّلاَةِ فَقَالَ «۝ أَقِيمُوا اَلصَّلاٰةَ وَ آتُوا اَلزَّكٰاةَ ۝» فَمَنْ أَقَامَ اَلصَّلاَةَ وَ لَمْ يُؤْتِ اَلزَّكَاةَ فَكَأَنَّهُ لَمْ يُقِمِ اَلصَّلاَةَ »."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.1584 - Ma'ruf ibn Kharrabudh reports from Abu Ja’far Imam Muhammad ibn Ali Al-Baqir (as) who said:\n\"Indeed, Allah (swt), Blessed and Exalted, has paired Zakat with prayer, as He said: 'Establish prayer and give Zakat' (Surah Al Baqarah 2:43). Therefore, whoever establishes prayer but does not give Zakat, it is as though he has not established prayer.\""
        ]
      }
